intro: The yellow bar is the pivot, the last item. `j` scans the other items. Everything in front of `i` is smaller than the pivot, so each smaller item `j` finds is swapped to `i`. At the end, the pivot swaps into place at `i`.
```python
def partition(items, lo, hi):
    pivot = items[hi]
    i = lo
    for j in range(lo, hi):
        if items[j] < pivot:
            items[i], items[j] = items[j], items[i]
            i += 1
