hint: Return `quicksort3(smaller) + equal + quicksort3(bigger)`.
hint: The equal items are already in place relative to each other, so they need no sorting.
right: All the items equal to the pivot are finished in one step, so a list with a few distinct values needs only a few levels.
wrong: Split the list into smaller, equal and bigger items, sort only the smaller and bigger lists, and join the three.

