=== task: multi medium
title: Good pivot choices
prompt: Quicksort sorts a list that's already sorted. Choose **every** pivot choice that avoids the O(n²) worst case on that list.
* A random item of the part :: Right. On average it lands near the middle, whatever the order.
* The median of the first, middle and last items :: Right. On sorted data that's the middle item, a perfect split.
* The middle item of the part :: Right. On sorted data the middle item is the median.
- The last item :: On sorted data it's always the biggest: n levels.
- The first item :: On sorted data it's always the smallest: n levels.
- The smallest item of the part :: The smallest item always gives an empty side, on any data.
hint: For each choice, where does the pivot land in a sorted part?
